# Build output
dist/
build/*
!build/sidecar.spec
*.exe
*.msi

# Fetched by setup.sh - too large to commit
.venv/
models/
assets/fonts/
!assets/commons/
*.onnx

# Generated media (samples are kept, see exception below)
*.mp4
*.wav
!samples/**/*.mp4
!samples/**/*.wav

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Node
node_modules/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
.venv-clone/
assets/voice/
# Clips set aside before re-recording. Same reason as above: these are
# hundreds of MB of audio, and a public repo is no place for a voice.
assets/voice-*/

# The live word list. The app writes the family's real names here - their
# child's name, their parents, their pets - and when the app runs from source
# this path is inside the repo. It was committed to a public repo once exactly
# that way, by a `git add -A` that had no idea it was publishing a child's
# name.
#
# What ships is sight-words.default.txt, with placeholder names. This file is
# seeded from it on first run and belongs to the family, not to git.
wordlists/sight-words.txt

# The starter voice DOES ship and IS tracked, unlike everything else under
# assets/ that holds audio. These are the developer's own 42 phoneme clips,
# shipped deliberately so a fresh install teaches with a human voice; a
# family's recordings (assets/voice/) still never leave their machine.
!assets/starter-voice/**/*.wav

# The family's own sentence library, like the live word list above: written
# by the app, holds their real sentences, never for git.
wordlists/sentences.txt
# The sight-word list typed in on the Sound Bank screen - a family's own
# words, same doctrine as sentences.txt: never committed.
wordlists/whole-words.txt
